 Well, but the language it is meant to be is a very delicate balance: logic=
al in a technical sense, monoparsed, and whatever else folks have added on.=
 =C2=A0A change in grammar will almost inevitably alter some of these thing=
s and restoring the balance will not be easy (and often not possible). =C2=
=A0It may be a better language in all sorts of ways (stripped of excrescenc=
es, say), but it will. not be the Lojban of the prospectus and so, arguably=
, not Lojban at all (name notwithstanding). =C2=A0pycyn

    On Tuesday, November 7, 2017, 6:16:12 PM CST, MorphemeAddict <lytlesw@g=
mail.com> wrote: =20
=20
 No, not "fall into ordinariness again". Rather, it will be improved to fix=
 or remove the problems discovered by the fluent speakers that weren't know=
n to the designers. A constant progression to a better language.=C2=A0
stevo=C2=A0

