On Tue, Nov 7, 2017 at 3:51 AM, <sukender1@gmail.com> wrote:

@stevo: Sorry I don't understand the "make it the same as it was before". F=
rom my point of view:  =20
   - Establishing language rules "forever" is not possible. Therefore some =
changes will be necessary. This is what called "evolution".
   - Forking may be interesting. It may be an pure experiment, a "feature b=
ranch", a fix, etc.
   - Reintegrating a branch to the core actually changes the core! This is =
why it must be done very carefully, in order to not break initial intents o=
f the language.
I hope I mad myself clearer :-)


